"q-moon-phases-0":{"target":{"node":"moon-phases","href":"../earth/astronomy/moon-phases/#step1"},"prompts":[{"node":"moon-phases","ask":{"zh":"月亮永远亮半边，为什么我们有时只看到一小部分亮面？","en":"The Moon is always half lit — so why do we sometimes see only a sliver of bright face?"}},{"node":"unit-circle","ask":{"zh":"把月亮绕地球的位置想成圆上的一个角，看到的亮面比例 (1 − cos θ)/2 在 θ 很小和 θ = 180° 时各是多少？","en":"Think of the Moon's position as an angle on a circle — what is the lit fraction (1 − cos θ)/2 when θ is tiny, and when θ = 180°?"}}],"reveal":{"zh":"亮面比例由月亮相对太阳的位置角决定，θ 从 0 变到 180°，亮面从 0 变到全部，大约 29.5 天一个周期。","en":"The lit fraction follows the Moon's angle relative to the Sun: as θ goes from 0 to 180°, the lit face grows from none to full, over a cycle of about 29.5 days."},"source":"../earth/astronomy/moon-phases/#step1","lesson":"moon-phases"},
"q-contour-lines-0":{"target":{"node":"contour-lines","href":"../earth/geo/contour-lines/#step1"},"prompts":[{"node":"contour-lines","ask":{"zh":"等高线越密，坡越陡还是越缓？相邻两条线之间，海拔差多少？","en":"Where contour lines crowd together, is the slope steeper or gentler? How much altitude changes between neighbouring lines?"}},{"node":"derivative","ask":{"zh":"水沿垂直于等高线的最陡方向往低处流——这个“最陡方向”和变化率有什么关系？","en":"Water runs downhill perpendicular to the contour lines, along the steepest direction — what does that steepest direction have to do with a rate of change?"}}],"reveal":{"zh":"等高线越密坡越陡，相邻线差一个等高距；水往最陡方向流，也就是高度变化最快的方向。","en":"Closer lines mean a steeper slope, with one contour interval between neighbours; water flows along the steepest descent, the direction where height changes fastest."},"source":"../earth/geo/contour-lines/#step1","lesson":"contour-lines"},
"q-latitude-longitude-0":{"target":{"node":"latitude-longitude","href":"../earth/geo/latitude-longitude/#step1"},"prompts":[{"node":"latitude-longitude","ask":{"zh":"纬线周长随 cos 纬度缩小——赤道和北纬 60° 的纬线圈，哪个长？长几倍？","en":"A parallel's length shrinks with cos(latitude) — which is longer, the equator or the 60° N parallel, and by what factor?"}},{"node":"unit-circle","ask":{"zh":"把地球想成单位圆上的角度：经度差 15° 对应几小时？为什么球面摊成平面必然变形？","en":"Think of the Earth in terms of angles on a circle — how many hours does 15° of longitude correspond to? And why must flattening a sphere distort it?"}}],"reveal":{"zh":"高纬纬线圈短得多，但地图常把它们拉长，所以显得特别大；15° 经度对应 1 小时，球面无法不经变形摊平。","en":"High-latitude parallels are much shorter, but maps stretch them, so they look huge; 15° of longitude is 1 hour, and a sphere cannot be flattened without distortion."},"source":"../earth/geo/latitude-longitude/#step1","lesson":"latitude-longitude"},
"q-seasons-orbit-0":{"target":{"node":"seasons-orbit","href":"../earth/astronomy/seasons-orbit/#step2"},"prompts":[{"node":"seasons-orbit","ask":{"zh":"地轴倾斜约 23.4° 且方向不变——一年里太阳直射点在南北回归线之间怎样移动？","en":"Earth's axis tilts about 23.4° in a fixed direction — how does the overhead point of the Sun move between the tropics over a year?"}},{"node":"sine","ask":{"zh":"直射点移动时，正午太阳高度和昼长怎样跟着变？这种变化像不像正弦波？","en":"As the overhead point moves, how do noon Sun height and day length change? Does that variation look like a sine wave?"}}],"reveal":{"zh":"直射点一年往返一次，正午高度和昼长随之周期变化，就是四季；日地距离只变约 3%，不是原因。","en":"The overhead point swings back and forth once a year, and noon height and day length vary with it — that is the seasons; the Earth-Sun distance varies only about 3% and is not the cause."},"source":"../earth/astronomy/seasons-orbit/#step2","lesson":"seasons-orbit"},
"q-atmospheric-circulation-0":{"target":{"node":"atmospheric-circulation","href":"../earth/climate/atmospheric-circulation/#step2"},"prompts":[{"node":"atmospheric-circulation","ask":{"zh":"赤道受热多，空气上升还是下沉？上升的空气冷却后，水汽会怎样？","en":"The equator is heated most — does air there rise or sink? What happens to its water vapour as it cools on rising?"}},{"node":"seasons-orbit","ask":{"zh":"空气在副热带下沉时，是变干还是变湿？下沉区对应多雨还是多沙漠？","en":"As air sinks in the subtropics, does it dry out or moisten? Does a sinking region mean rain or desert?"}}],"reveal":{"zh":"赤道空气上升冷却，水汽凝结成雨；空气流到副热带下沉增温，抑制成云，所以副热带多沙漠。","en":"Equatorial air rises and cools, condensing its vapour into rain; by the subtropics the air sinks and warms, suppressing clouds — hence deserts."},"source":"../earth/climate/atmospheric-circulation/#step2","lesson":"atmospheric-circulation"},
